---
// The privacy policy (Google Play needs its URL). Every claim here is checked against the
// code: keep it true when the app, the relay or the hosting changes (AGENTS.md "No
// telemetry", relay retention in crates/zafe-relay, Caddy's "no access log").
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = '22 October 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy · Zafe"
  description="What Zafe keeps on your phone, what leaves it, and who can see what."
  bodyClass="legal-page"
>
  <Nav links={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home', mobile: true, back: true }]} />
  <main class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Zafe is a shielded multisig wallet for Zcash, made by Anmol Bansal, a sole
      proprietorship in India ("we"). It is non-custodial: your key share never leaves your
      phone, and we can't see or move your funds. There are no accounts, no analytics, no
      ads and no tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your key share and vault keys, in the phone's secure storage (backed by the Android Keystore).</li>
      <li>Your vaults' balances and payment history, in an encrypted database.</li>
      <li>The names you give vaults and co-signers on this phone.</li>
      <li>
        A log of errors, with addresses, amounts and other personal details removed. It
        leaves your phone only if you share it yourself, from Settings.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What leaves your phone, and who can see it</h2>

    <h3>The relay (run by us)</h3>
    <p>
      The members of a vault reach each other through a relay. It passes on messages and
      keeps the vault's history so every member sees the same payments. The relay sees:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Each member's public keys, and messages and history that are end-to-end encrypted
        between the vault's members. It can't read them. It does see their size and when
        they were sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you allow notifications, a notification token, so it can wake your phone through
        Google's Firebase Cloud Messaging. Notifications carry no content.
      </li>
      <li>
        The name you give yourself in a vault, encrypted like the rest of the history.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The relay keeps no access logs and doesn't record IP addresses. It uses them only
      briefly, in memory, to limit abuse. Messages waiting for a member are deleted once
      picked up, and in any case after 30 days; recovery checks after 7 days. A vault's
      encrypted history is kept while the vault exists, and a setup that is cancelled is
      deleted. We keep backups of the relay's data to recover from failures.
    </p>

    <h3>The Zcash server</h3>
    <p>
      To show balances and send payments, the app talks to a public Zcash server (Zec.rocks
      by default; you can choose another, or your own, in Settings). Like any Zcash wallet, it
      downloads blocks and pending transactions and submits your vault's signed transactions.
      The server sees your IP address and when you connect. It doesn't receive your keys or
      your vault's viewing key.
    </p>

    <h3>Prices</h3>
    <p>
      The mainnet app shows dollar values. It asks CoinGecko for the ZEC price, or, with Tor
      on, several exchanges through Tor. The request contains nothing about you or your vault.
    </p>

    <h3>Tor</h3>
    <p>
      With "Use Tor" on (Settings), the app reaches the relay, the Zcash server and price
      sources through Tor, so they don't see your IP address. Notifications still arrive
      through Google.
    </p>

    <h3>Google Play</h3>
    <p>
      If you installed Zafe from Google Play, the app asks Play whether an update is
      available. Google's privacy policy applies to Play.
    </p>

    <h2>Camera, backups, unlock</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The camera is used only to scan QR codes (invites, addresses). Nothing is recorded or sent.</li>
      <li>
        Backups you export are encrypted with your backup words and saved where you choose.
        We never receive them, and we can't recover your words.
      </li>
      <li>Fingerprint or screen-lock checks are done by your phone; Zafe never sees them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="waitlist">The iPhone waitlist</h2>
    <p>
      If you join the iPhone waitlist on this website, we store your email address and the
      time you joined, in a private store at Vercel, which hosts the website. We use it only
      to send you one email when Zafe is out for iPhone, then we delete the list. To have
      your address deleted sooner, write to the address below.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics, crash reporting, advertising or tracking libraries, in the app or on the
      website. We don't sell or share data, and the app has no account of yours to delete:
      removing a vault from the app deletes its data from your phone.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Zafe isn't meant for anyone under 18.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>When this policy changes, we update this page and its date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:privacy@zafe.cash">privacy@zafe.cash</a></p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
